      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.25,
          "end": 5.7,
          "en": "And that's it for this course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.7,
          "end": 9.54,
          "en": "In this course section, we built this Flutter learning quiz,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.54,
          "end": 13.05,
          "en": "where we can answer Flutter related questions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.05,
          "end": 15.27,
          "en": "And after we answer these questions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.27,
          "end": 16.86,
          "en": "we get this result screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.86,
          "end": 20.58,
          "en": "where we can see which questions were answered correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.58,
          "end": 23.04,
          "en": "And which answers would've been the correct answers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.04,
          "end": 25.62,
          "en": "for the different questions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.62,
          "end": 27.18,
          "en": "From this results screen, we can then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.18,
          "end": 29.16,
          "en": "of course, also restart the quiz,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.16,
          "end": 32.79,
          "en": "and give it another try where we might do better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.79,
          "end": 34.38,
          "en": "Now, whilst building this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.38,
          "end": 38.58,
          "en": "we again learned way more about Flutter and also Dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.58,
          "end": 41.01,
          "en": "We, of course, used the knowledge we already gained",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.01,
          "end": 43.14,
          "en": "in the previous course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.14,
          "end": 45.75,
          "en": "For example, the knowledge that this main function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.75,
          "end": 48.3,
          "en": "in the main .dart file is the main entry point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.3,
          "end": 50.49,
          "en": "since it's executed automatically by Dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.49,
          "end": 51.9,
          "en": "when the app starts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.9,
          "end": 54.06,
          "en": "And that you must then call runApp",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.06,
          "end": 56.31,
          "en": "and pass your widget tree to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 56.31,
          "end": 59.79,
          "en": "But in this section, we built way more widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 59.79,
          "end": 62.28,
          "en": "We passed data around between those widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.28,
          "end": 65.79,
          "en": "including more complex data like functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 65.79,
          "end": 68.73,
          "en": "In this section, you learned that in your widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 68.73,
          "end": 72.3,
          "en": "you can actually also accept functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 72.3,
          "end": 75.36,
          "en": "as input values, as arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.36,
          "end": 79.8,
          "en": "And that you can then use these functions in your widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.8,
          "end": 82.35,
          "en": "for example, to bind them to buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.35,
          "end": 84.53999999999999,
          "en": "And that you can therefore also create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.53999999999999,
          "end": 87.78,
          "en": "and then set those functions as values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.78,
          "end": 90.48,
          "en": "for those arguments that want functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 90.48,
          "end": 93.66,
          "en": "You learn that you can pass functions as values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 93.66,
          "end": 97.35,
          "en": "which is a crucial pattern that will be needed quite a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.35,
          "end": 99.663,
          "en": "when building more complex Flutter apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 100.86,
          "end": 104.31,
          "en": "You also learned that you can output conditional content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.31,
          "end": 107.4,
          "en": "with help of the if keyword, for example, which allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.4,
          "end": 111.50999999999999,
          "en": "to set a variable in this case here to different values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.50999999999999,
          "end": 114.47999999999999,
          "en": "based on different state values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.47999999999999,
          "end": 116.61,
          "en": "And then this variable can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.61,
          "end": 118.25999999999999,
          "en": "to output it in the widget tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.25999999999999,
          "end": 121.62,
          "en": "And therefore, since the variable contains different values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.62,
          "end": 123.66,
          "en": "based on different state values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.66,
          "end": 126.96,
          "en": "the UI looks different for those different states.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.96,
          "end": 130.2,
          "en": "And that's exactly what conditional content is all about,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 130.2,
          "end": 133.83,
          "en": "having different UI states for different conditions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.83,
          "end": 136.17000000000002,
          "en": "You did also not just learn about the if statement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136.17000000000002,
          "end": 139.38,
          "en": "which is a great way of setting content conditionally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.38,
          "end": 142.32,
          "en": "but you also learned about using ternary expressions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 142.32,
          "end": 144.63,
          "en": "which gives you a more concise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.63,
          "end": 147.87,
          "en": "but sometimes also harder to read and understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.87,
          "end": 150.54,
          "en": "way of setting content conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 150.54,
          "end": 153,
          "en": "And you even learned that you could manage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 153,
          "end": 156,
          "en": "entire widgets as state values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 156,
          "end": 157.32,
          "en": "Though you also learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 157.32,
          "end": 159.63,
          "en": "that this can have some disadvantages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 159.63,
          "end": 162.66,
          "en": "especially if those widgets then must receive some data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 162.66,
          "end": 165.66,
          "en": "like for example, a pointer at a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 165.66,
          "end": 168.21,
          "en": "But you learned about these different approaches.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 168.21,
          "end": 170.97,
          "en": "And you did also not just learn about if statements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 170.97,
          "end": 173.37,
          "en": "but also about for loops,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 173.37,
          "end": 176.46,
          "en": "which is another crucial Dart concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 176.46,
          "end": 180.18,
          "en": "Actually a feature you find in many programming languages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 180.18,
          "end": 182.64,
          "en": "as it allows you to execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 182.64,
          "end": 185.1,
          "en": "the same piece of code repeatedly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 185.1,
          "end": 188.16,
          "en": "until some condition is not met anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 188.16,
          "end": 191.97,
          "en": "And here we use the for loop to go through all the answers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 191.97,
          "end": 196.97,
          "en": "chosen by a user, and create some summary data pieces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 197.01,
          "end": 199.05,
          "en": "based on these answers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 199.05,
          "end": 203.55,
          "en": "And these summary data pieces were actually so-called maps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 203.55,
          "end": 206.73,
          "en": "Another built in value type in Dart,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 206.73,
          "end": 210.06,
          "en": "which allows you to quickly combine different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 210.06,
          "end": 213.54,
          "en": "key value pairs into one object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 213.54,
          "end": 217.02,
          "en": "The alternative would've been to build a custom class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 217.02,
          "end": 219.42000000000002,
          "en": "as a blueprint for a custom object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 219.42000000000002,
          "end": 222.6,
          "en": "And this would've also yielded various benefits,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 222.6,
          "end": 225.09,
          "en": "especially regarding type safety,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 225.09,
          "end": 227.55,
          "en": "because you did see that when using a map,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 227.55,
          "end": 231.24,
          "en": "you have to do a lot of type casting to tell Dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 231.24,
          "end": 233.55,
          "en": "which type of value is stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 233.55,
          "end": 236.52,
          "en": "under a specific key in such a map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 236.52,
          "end": 238.26,
          "en": "But it's nonetheless very important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 238.26,
          "end": 242.19,
          "en": "to know about this map value, since you will also encounter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 242.19,
          "end": 245.85,
          "en": "and use that quite a bit when working with Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 245.85,
          "end": 248.67,
          "en": "In addition to these Dart features and patterns,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 248.67,
          "end": 252.12,
          "en": "we also learned about some new widgets, like for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 252.12,
          "end": 254.49,
          "en": "the single child scroll view widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 254.49,
          "end": 257.79,
          "en": "which can be used to make its child widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 257.79,
          "end": 260.46,
          "en": "often a column, scrollable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 260.46,
          "end": 263.79,
          "en": "Which is something we use here on this final results page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 263.79,
          "end": 266.16,
          "en": "to make this box in the middle here scrollable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 266.16,
          "end": 271.02,
          "en": "whilst still restricting it in size, in height specifically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 271.02,
          "end": 273.72,
          "en": "You also saw some new configuration items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 273.72,
          "end": 276.87,
          "en": "and styling options in action, like for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 276.87,
          "end": 279.63,
          "en": "the shape option for elevated buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 279.63,
          "end": 281.90999999999997,
          "en": "to add rounded borders to the button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 281.90999999999997,
          "end": 285.03,
          "en": "And in general you, of course, saw many examples",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 285.03,
          "end": 289.08,
          "en": "for the usage and configuration of various Flutter widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 289.08,
          "end": 291.45,
          "en": "Last, but not least, in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 291.45,
          "end": 293.88,
          "en": "we also used the class keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 293.88,
          "end": 297.27,
          "en": "for something else than a custom widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 297.27,
          "end": 300.78,
          "en": "Of course, you will very often create custom widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 300.78,
          "end": 304.59,
          "en": "stateless widgets, or stateful widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 304.59,
          "end": 307.26,
          "en": "But in Dart, you can also use the class keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 307.26,
          "end": 310.77,
          "en": "to build standard classes, standard blueprints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 310.77,
          "end": 314.67,
          "en": "for standard objects that don't act as widgets to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 314.67,
          "end": 317.61,
          "en": "for example, build a blueprint for an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 317.61,
          "end": 321.51,
          "en": "that contains the question text and its possible answers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 321.51,
          "end": 325.35,
          "en": "As well as a utility method for shuffling those answers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 325.35,
          "end": 328.71,
          "en": "and returning a new list of shuffled answers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 328.71,
          "end": 332.4,
          "en": "That is what we used a custom class for in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 332.4,
          "end": 335.37,
          "en": "And speaking of shuffling answers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 335.37,
          "end": 338.64,
          "en": "in this section you also learned about various methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 338.64,
          "end": 340.74,
          "en": "that can be called on lists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 340.74,
          "end": 344.04,
          "en": "to manipulate or analyze those lists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 344.04,
          "end": 346.77,
          "en": "For example, the shuffle method, which can be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 346.77,
          "end": 349.92,
          "en": "on a list to change the order of list items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 349.92,
          "end": 354.42,
          "en": "But also, the add method to add new entries to a list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 354.42,
          "end": 357.03,
          "en": "And the where method to filter a list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 357.03,
          "end": 360.51,
          "en": "to create a new list that only contains the list entries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 360.51,
          "end": 363.12,
          "en": "where a certain condition is met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 363.12,
          "end": 365.64,
          "en": "In addition, you also learned about the map method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 365.64,
          "end": 368.55,
          "en": "which can also be called on a list to generate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 368.55,
          "end": 372.15,
          "en": "a new list of transformed list items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 372.15,
          "end": 374.64,
          "en": "which we, for example, used to transform",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 374.64,
          "end": 376.86,
          "en": "our list of string answers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 376.86,
          "end": 379.743,
          "en": "to a list of tapable answer button widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 380.67,
          "end": 384.54,
          "en": "You also learned about this special spread operator here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 384.54,
          "end": 387.45,
          "en": "the three dots operator, which can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 387.45,
          "end": 390.63,
          "en": "to pull all the list elements out of a list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 390.63,
          "end": 394.35,
          "en": "and add them as standalone comma separated items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 394.35,
          "end": 395.94,
          "en": "to a surrounding list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 395.94,
          "end": 397.83,
          "en": "In this case here, used to get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
